course: dictionary
lesson: 11939
title: Canned: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Canned is one of them. «We ate canned peaches for pudding.» Peaches in a tin are kept in a sealed metal can, so canned means tinned here.
explain: Now read this: «The laughter in the sitcom was canned.» Nobody in the room laughed at that moment. The laughter was recorded earlier and played again. Ask yourself: does the meaning fit the sentence? Swap in "tinned" and the sentence makes no sense, so you need the recorded meaning.
explain: Canned can also be informal. «Sam got canned from his job at the shop» means he lost his job. «The new show was canned after one series» means it was stopped. In both cases, the context tells you the meaning, so you do not need to panic when you meet an unknown use.
fact: Canned means kept in a sealed metal can or tin, like canned beans or canned peaches.
fact: Canned laughter is laughter that was recorded earlier and played again, not live.
fact: Informal: got canned means lost a job (mostly used in the US), and a canned show is one that was stopped or cancelled.
fact: Canned is also the past form of the verb can, which means to put food into tins: «Mum canned the tomatoes in August.»
fact: To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right one.
exercise: «We ate canned peaches for pudding.» What does canned mean here? | Fresh from the tree | Frozen solid | *Kept in a sealed tin | Cooked in a pan on the hob
exercise: «The laughter in the sitcom was canned.» What is canned laughter? | Laughter from a live crowd in the room | Laughter that is very loud and rude | *Laughter recorded earlier and played again
exercise: «Sam got canned from his job at the shop.» What does got canned mean? | *Lost his job | Moved house | Was given a new job | Won a prize
test: «The new show was canned after one series.» What does canned mean here? | Repeated every night | Made into a film | *Cancelled, stopped | Played live
test: Which sentence uses canned to mean recorded, not live? | We ate canned soup for lunch. | Mum canned the peaches in August. | Grandpa has a can of cola. | *The show had canned laughter after every joke.
exam: In «The show got canned after one series», what does canned mean? | Filled with food | Praised | *Cancelled, stopped | Recorded
